    {
      "date": "1995-10-12",
      "kind": "planning decision",
      "description": "Having upheld its negative declaration, the City Planning Commission approved with conditions, 4-0, a four-storey building of about 4,990 square feet of shops and 19 dwellings over basement parking on the 11,485-square-foot site beside the Bell Markets parking lot, setting aside two units as affordable and barring a retail coffee store or any single tenant over 2,499 square feet without further approval (Motion 13973).",
